 "立ちどころに": "حَالاً (Immediately; now; right away.)  [at once]\nمثال: 悪運続きという目にあったので、私の財産は、たちどころに、ついえさってしまった。\n→ Having hit a streak of bad luck, my fortune had gone to pot in no time.",
 "立ちなおる": "[to regain one's footing ; to get back on one's feet]\nمثال: ショックから立ち直りましたか。\n→ Have you recovered from the shock? / شُفِيَ, بَرِئَ (To get better, to regain health or prosperity.)  [to recover]",
 "立ちゆく": "آخِر (Final, ultimate, coming after all others of its kind.) / مَاضٍ, الْمَاضِي (Most recent, latest, last so far.) / آخر (after everything else; finally) / اِسْتَمَرَّ, دَامَ (To endure, continue over time.)  [to last]",
 "立ちんぼ": "[streetwalker ; street girl] / [being kept standing (without doing anything) ; remaining on one's feet] / سَائِل (A person who begs.) / فَقِير (A person suffering from extreme poverty.)  [beggar] / [tout (for a hostess bar)]",
 "立ちん坊": "[streetwalker ; street girl] / [being kept standing (without doing anything) ; remaining on one's feet] / سَائِل (A person who begs.) / فَقِير (A person suffering from extreme poverty.)  [beggar] / [tout (for a hostess bar)]",
 "立ち上がり": "نَجْمَة, اِبْتِدَاء (The beginning of an activity.) / نَجْمَة (The beginning point of a race, a board game, etc.) / بَدَأَ (To begin, commence, initiate.)  [start] / [how well a pitcher pitches at the start of the game]",
 "立ち上がる": "قَامَ (To rise from a lying or sitting position.)  [to stand up]\nمثال: 突然若い女性が立ち上がった。\n→ Suddenly, a young woman stood up. / شُفِيَ, بَرِئَ (To get better, to regain health or prosperity.)  [to recover] / نَجْمَة, اِبْتِدَاء (The beginning of an activity.) / نَجْمَة (The beginning point of a race, a board game, etc.) / بَدَأَ (To begin, commence, initiate.)  [to start (doing)]\nمثال: 多くの消費者は消費税反対に立ち上がった。\n→ Many consumers rose up against the consumption tax. / [to rise (from a crouch) and make the initial charge]",
 "立ち上げる": "نَجْمَة, اِبْتِدَاء (The beginning of an activity.) / نَجْمَة (The beginning point of a race, a board game, etc.) / بَدَأَ (To begin, commence, initiate.)  [to start (something)]\nمثال: あの会社もついにホームページを立ち上げたらしい。\n→ That company just put up a web page. / جَزْمَة (heavy shoe that covers part of the leg) / بسطار (heavy shoe that covers part of the leg)  [to boot (a computer)]\nمثال: ノートパソコンの電源を入れ、ブラウザを立ち上げて、もう覚えてしまったアドレスを打ち込む。\n→ I switch on my laptop, start up the browser, and type in the address I've already learnt by heart.",
 "立ち上り": "نَجْمَة, اِبْتِدَاء (The beginning of an activity.) / نَجْمَة (The beginning point of a race, a board game, etc.) / بَدَأَ (To begin, commence, initiate.)  [start] / [how well a pitcher pitches at the start of the game]",
 "立ち上る": "نَهَضَ, اِرْتَفْعَ (To move, or appear to move, physically upwards relative to the ground.) / أَشْرَقَ, شَرَقَ (To move, or appear to move, physically upwards relative to the ground.)  [to rise (of smoke, steam, etc.)]\nمثال: 彼は立ち上るように言われ、ゆっくりとそうした。\n→ He was told to stand up, and he did so slowly.",
