 "立ち会い": "حُضُور (The fact or condition of being present, or of being within sight or call, or at )  [presence (e.g. of an observer)] / [trading session (at an exchange)] / [rising from a crouch to charge ; initial charge]\nesp. 立ち合い",
 "立ち会う": "حَضَرَ ((''ambitransitive'') to be present at or regularly go to)  [to attend]",
 "立ち位置": "مَوْقِع, مَكَان (A place or location.) / مَنْصِب (A post of employment; a job.) / مَكَانَة, رُتْبَة (A status or rank.) / رَأْي, مَوْقِف (An opinion, stand, or stance.) / جِلْسَة, وَقْفَة (A posture.)  [position (where one is standing)] / مَوْقِع, مَكَان (A place or location.) / مَنْصِب (A post of employment; a job.) / مَكَانَة, رُتْبَة (A status or rank.) / رَأْي, مَوْقِف (An opinion, stand, or stance.) / جِلْسَة, وَقْفَة (A posture.)  [position]",
 "立ち入り": "أَدْخَلَ (To cause to go (into), or to be received (into); to put in; to insert; to cause ) / أَدْخَلَ (To type (something) into a computer; to input.) / دَخَلَ (To go into or upon, as lands, and take actual possession of them.)  [entering]\nمثال: 部外者の立ち入りを禁ず。\n→ No outsiders are allowed to enter.",
 "立ち入り禁止": "مَمْنُوع الدُّخُولُ (Used on signs to indicate that entry into the area where the sign is displayed i)  [No Entry]\non a sign\nمثال: この建物は、現在立ち入り禁止だ。\n→ This building is off limits now. / حَدَّ, حَدَّدَ (To restrain within boundaries; to limit; to confine)  [restricted]",
 "立ち入る": "أَدْخَلَ (To cause to go (into), or to be received (into); to put in; to insert; to cause ) / أَدْخَلَ (To type (something) into a computer; to input.) / دَخَلَ (To go into or upon, as lands, and take actual possession of them.)  [to enter]\nمثال: 警察は彼の生活に立ち入って調べ上げた。\n→ The police raked through his life. / [to meddle (in) ; to interfere (in)] / [to go deeply (into an issue) ; to delve deeper (into)]",
 "立ち到る": "بَلَغَ (To extend, stretch, or thrust out (for example a limb or object held in the hand)  [to reach]\nمثال: 彼はこれまでこんな苦境に立ち至ったことはなかった。\n→ Never in his life had he encountered such a dilemma.",
 "立ち勝る": "فَاقَ, تَجَاوَزَ (To go beyond or exceed (something) in an adjudicative or literal sense.)  [to surpass]",
 "立ち去る": "تَرَكَ (To have a consequence or remnant.) / تَرَكَ, غَادَرَ (To depart; to separate from.) / إِجَازَة, عُطْلَة (Permission to be absent; time away from one's work.)  [to leave]\nمثال: 私は彼の墓を立ち去り難かった。\n→ I hesitated to leave his grave.",
 "立ち合い": "حُضُور (The fact or condition of being present, or of being within sight or call, or at )  [presence (e.g. of an observer)] / [trading session (at an exchange)] / [rising from a crouch to charge ; initial charge]\nesp. 立ち合い",
 "立ち向かう": "عَارَض (To attempt to stop the progression of; to resist or antagonize by physical means) / اِعْتَرَضَ (To object to.)  [to oppose]\nمثال: 彼女は自分の運命に立ち向かう覚悟ができていた。\n→ She was ready to face her fate.",
 "立ち回り": "عَارَكَ, قَاتَلَ (Senses relating to physical conflict:) / تَعَارَكَ, تَقَاتَلَ (Senses relating to physical conflict:) / نَاضَلَ, كَافَحَ (To strive for something; to campaign or contend for success.) / قِتَال (An occasion of fighting.) / مَعْرَكَة (A battle between opposing armies.)  [fight] / [walking about ; walking around] / [conducting oneself] / تَجَوُّل, تَنَزُّه (A wandering on foot; an idle and leisurely walk; a ramble; a saunter.) / تَجَوَّلَ, تَنَزَّهَ (To wander on foot; to ramble idly or leisurely; to rove.)  [stroll (in noh, an action piece involving circling the stage)]",
 "立ち回る": "[to walk about ; to walk around] / عَمَل (Something done, a deed.) / قَانُون ((In the United States) A legislative proposal, a bill that has not yet become la) / مَثَّلَ (To perform a theatrical role.) / تَصَرَّفَ (To behave in a certain manner for an indefinite length of time.)  [to act] / [to stop by (somewhere; esp. of a criminal on the run) ; to drop by] / [to enact a fighting scene ; to brawl (in a play, film, etc.)]",
 "立ち売り": "جَوَّال, بَائِع مُتَجَوِّل (An itinerant seller of small goods.)  [peddler]",
 "立ち寄る": "[to drop by ; to stop by]\nمثال: 夕方会社にお立ち寄りください。\n→ Drop by my office this evening. / اِقْتَرَبَ (To come or go near, in place or time; to move toward; to advance nearer; to draw) / اِقْتِرَاب, مُقَارَبَة (An act of drawing near in place or time; an advancing or coming near.) / كَيْفِيَّة, طَرِيقَة (A manner of making (a policy) or solving (a problem, etc.).)  [to approach]",
 "立ち居": "حَرَكَة (Physical motion between points in space.) / حَرَكَة (A trend in various fields or social categories, a group of people with a common )  [movements]",
 "立ち居振る舞い": "حَرَكَة (Physical motion between points in space.) / حَرَكَة (A trend in various fields or social categories, a group of people with a common )  [movements]",
 "立ち居振舞い": "حَرَكَة (Physical motion between points in space.) / حَرَكَة (A trend in various fields or social categories, a group of people with a common )  [movements]",
 "立ち帰る": "عَادَ, رَجَعَ (To return to a place.)  [to come back (to)]\nمثال: 面倒なようでも、基本に立ち返って検討し直したらどうだろう。急がば回れ、というじゃない。\n→ It may seem like a hassle, but I think you ought to go back to the basics and start over. Haste makes waste they say.",
 "立ち往生": "مَعْلِف, مُرَاح (A compartment for a single animal in a stable or cattle shed.) / بَسْطة (A small open-fronted shop, for example in a market, food court, etc.)  [stalling]\nمثال: 私は病院へ行く途中、交通渋滞にあって立ち往生してしまった。\n→ I was held up on my way to the hospital in a traffic jam. / [being stumped ; being in a dilemma]\nمثال: フランス語の先生は生徒の質問に立ち往生した。\n→ The French teacher was stumped by her student's question. / [dying while standing (and remaining standing) ; dying on one's feet]",
 "立ち戻る": "رَجَعَ, عَادَ (To come or go back (to a place or person).) / أَرْجَعَ, أَعَادَ (To give something back to its original holder or owner.) / عَوْدَة (The act of returning.)  [to return]",
