 "結核": "سُلّ (An infectious disease of humans and animals caused by a species of mycobacterium)  [tuberculosis]\nمثال: 何年か前には、結核にかかっていると知らされることは死の宣告を聞くのに等しかった。\n→ Some years ago, learning that one had tuberculosis amounted to hearing a sentence of death. / [concretion]",
 "結核症": "سُلّ (An infectious disease of humans and animals caused by a species of mycobacterium)  [tuberculosis]",
 "結構": "حَسَّن, لَطِيف (Pleasant, satisfactory, complimentary.)  [nice]\nمثال: 好奇心がお旺盛なのは大変に結構なことである。\n→ A healthy curiosity is truly a fine thing. / كَافٍ (sufficient) / تَمَامًا (Sufficiently.) / مَه, كَفَى (Stop! Don't do that any more! It is too much!)  [enough]\nمثال: どちらの日でも結構です。\n→ Either day is OK. / غَرَامَة (A fee levied as punishment for breaking the law.) / غَرَّمَ (To issue a fine as punishment to (someone).)  [fine (as in \"I'm fine\")]\nمثال: いや結構です。たくさんいただきました。\n→ No more, thank you. I'm full. / بِالْأَحْرَى (Used to specify a choice or preference; preferably, in preference to. (Now usual)  [rather]\nمثال: 彼女の髪の毛は結構短い。\n→ The woman's hair is quite short.",
