 "美味い": "مَاهِر, حَاذِق (Possessing skill; skilled.)  [skillful]\nesp. 上手い, 巧い\nمثال: 彼女はテニスは上手いが、水泳は下手だ。\n→ She's very good at tennis, but she's not much of a swimmer. / لَذِيذ (pleasing to taste) / شَهِيّ (pleasing to taste)  [delicious]\nesp. 旨い, 美味い, 甘い\nمثال: あそこの食べ物はうまいし値段も安いが、地の利が悪いのが難点だね。\n→ That place's food is great, and their prices are good, but the fly in the ointment is their terrible location. / حَسَن, جَيِّد (Of a person or an animal:) / حَسَن, جَيِّد (Of a capability:) / صِحِّيّ (Of a property or quality:) / حَسَنًا (That is good; an elliptical exclamation of satisfaction or commendation.) / خَيْر (The forces or behaviours that are the enemy of evil. Usually consists of helping) / سِلْعَة (An item of merchandise.)  [good (deal, idea, etc.)]\nesp. 旨い\nمثال: それはあまりにもうますぎる話だ。\n→ That's too good a story to be true.",
