 "考える": "فَكَرَ, فَكَّرَ (To ponder, to go over in one's mind.) / فَكَّرَ (To communicate to oneself in one's mind, to try to find a solution to a problem.) / ظَنَّ (To guess; to reckon; to believe while admittedly being uncertain.)  [to think (about, of)]\nمثال: あなたは家族の事を考えるべきです。\n→ You must think of your family. / اِعْتَبَرَ, تَدَبَّرَ (To think about seriously.) / عَدَّ (To assign some quality to.)  [to consider]\nمثال: 人々を幸福にするのは何なのかを考えることは価値がある。\n→ It is worthwhile considering what it is that makes people happy. / فَكَرَ, فَكَّرَ (To ponder, to go over in one's mind.) / فَكَّرَ (To communicate to oneself in one's mind, to try to find a solution to a problem.) / ظَنَّ (To guess; to reckon; to believe while admittedly being uncertain.)  [to think (that)]\nمثال: 私たちは人をその人の人格を基に判断しようと考えるかもしれないが、それらは一見したところでははっきりわからないものである。\n→ Although we may intend to judge a person on the basis of his or her personal qualities, they are not visible at first sight. / تَعَمَّدَ, نَوَى (To fix the mind upon (something, or something to be accomplished); be intent upo)  [to intend (to do)]\nمثال: それほど多くの人々のための料理の献立を考えるのはむずかしい。\n→ It is difficult planning meals for so many people.",
