 "聞える": "[to be heard ; to be audible]\nمثال: 妙な音が聞こえた。\n→ I heard a strange sound. / سليم (Healthy.) / صَوْت, صوت (A sensation perceived by the ear caused by the vibration of air or some other me) / صَوَّتَ, طَلَّع صوت (To produce a sound.)  [to sound (like)]\nمثال: この話は、変に聞こえるかもしれないが、全く本当です。\n→ This story may sound strange, but it's absolutely true. / [to be well known ; to be famous] / قَبِلَ (To receive, especially with a consent, with favour, or with approval.) / اِعْتَرَفَ (To admit to a place or a group.) / قَبِلَ (To receive or admit to; to agree to; to assent to; to submit to.)  [to accept (someone's words)]",
 "聞かす": "أَخْبَرَ, قَالَ (Social senses of communicating) / تَلّ (A hill or mound, originally and especially in the Middle East, over or consistin)  [to tell (e.g. a story)]\nمثال: そのことについてできるだけ話を聞かしてください。\n→ Tell me as much about that as possible. / [to make (someone) listen ; to make (someone) understand] / [to grip (someone) with skilful singing, storytelling, etc. ; to hold (someone) enchanted by]",
 "聞かせる": "أَخْبَرَ, قَالَ (Social senses of communicating) / تَلّ (A hill or mound, originally and especially in the Middle East, over or consistin)  [to tell (e.g. a story)]\nمثال: 助けを求めている私の声を彼に聞かせるのに苦労した。\n→ I had trouble making him hear me calling for help. / [to make (someone) listen ; to make (someone) understand]\nمثال: あの男を説き伏せようとするのは、オオカミに道理を説いて聞かせるようなものだ。\n→ You might as well reason with the wolf as try to persuade that man. / [to grip (someone) with skilful singing, storytelling, etc. ; to hold (someone) enchanted by]",
 "聞かぬ気": "مُتَوَحِّش, خارج عن السيطرَة (Wild; uncontrolled.)  [unruly (e.g. of a child)]",
 "聞かん気": "مُتَوَحِّش, خارج عن السيطرَة (Wild; uncontrolled.)  [unruly (e.g. of a child)]",
 "聞き": "سَمِيع (Able to hear, as opposed to deaf.) / سَمْع (The sense used to perceive sound.) / جَلْسَة (A proceeding at which discussions are heard.) / جَلْسَة (A legal procedure done before a judge, without a jury, as with an evidentiary he)  [hearing] / إِشَاعَة, شَائِعَة (A statement or claim of questionable accuracy, from no known reliable source, us)  [rumor] / مَذَاق (The taking of a small amount of food or drink into the mouth in order to taste i)  [tasting (alcohol, tea, etc.)]",
