 "聞こえる": "[to be heard ; to be audible]\nمثال: 妙な音が聞こえた。\n→ I heard a strange sound. / سليم (Healthy.) / صَوْت, صوت (A sensation perceived by the ear caused by the vibration of air or some other me) / صَوَّتَ, طَلَّع صوت (To produce a sound.)  [to sound (like)]\nمثال: この話は、変に聞こえるかもしれないが、全く本当です。\n→ This story may sound strange, but it's absolutely true. / [to be well known ; to be famous] / قَبِلَ (To receive, especially with a consent, with favour, or with approval.) / اِعْتَرَفَ (To admit to a place or a group.) / قَبِلَ (To receive or admit to; to agree to; to assent to; to submit to.)  [to accept (someone's words)]",
 "聞こし召す": "سَمِع (To perceive sounds through the ear.)  [to hear] / شَرِبَ, شرب (To consume (a liquid) through the mouth.) / شَرَاب, مَشْرُوب (A beverage.) / شراب (Alcoholic beverages in general.)  [to drink]",
