 "聲": "صَوْت, صوت (Sound uttered by the mouth, especially by human beings in speech or song; sound ) / صَوْت, صوت (Sound made through vibration of the vocal cords; sonant, or intonated, utterance) / صَوَّت (To vote; to elect; to appoint)  [voice]\nمثال: あなたの声が聞けてうれしいわ。\n→ I am happy to hear your voice. / غِنَاء (The act of using the voice to produce musical sounds; vocalizing.)  [singing (of a bird)]\nمثال: 日本人は鳥や虫の声を楽しむ。\n→ The Japanese enjoy the songs of birds and insects. / صَوْت, صوت (Sound uttered by the mouth, especially by human beings in speech or song; sound ) / صَوْت, صوت (Sound made through vibration of the vocal cords; sonant, or intonated, utterance) / صَوَّت (To vote; to elect; to appoint)  [voice]\nمثال: どこの国でも、何時の時代でも、子供は親の価値観を見習って育つものである。いわゆる「教育ママ」の教育に対する考え方が、子供を精神的にいびつに育ててしまっていると指摘する声もある。\n→ As children are known to emulate the values of adults, it is often pointed out such \"education mamas\" instill a warped sense of values in… / سليم (Healthy.) / صَوْت, صوت (A sensation perceived by the ear caused by the vibration of air or some other me) / صَوَّتَ, طَلَّع صوت (To produce a sound.)  [sound]",
 "聳える": "نَهَضَ, اِرْتَفْعَ (To move, or appear to move, physically upwards relative to the ground.) / أَشْرَقَ, شَرَقَ (To move, or appear to move, physically upwards relative to the ground.)  [to rise (of a building, mountain, etc.)]\nمثال: その峰は雲の上にそびえている。\n→ The peak rises above the clouds.",
